WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.467
Five unfair advantages.

2
00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:06.600
These are ways to stand out as the candidate nobody else can offer.

3
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.267
You do not need all five.

4
00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.600
You need one, executed visibly.

5
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:13.867
Here are the five.

6
00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:18.633
The evaluation engineer, who can explain exactly how quality is measured.

7
00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:22.367
The cost optimization expert, who saves lakhs a month.

8
00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:29.000
The agentic architect, who builds bounded autonomy, with humans approving consequential actions.

9
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:35.367
The domain specialist, who combines AI with a vertical like legaltech, fintech or field service.

10
00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:40.500
And the inference systems engineer, the highest paid intersection and the hardest to fake.

11
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.870
Cost shows how concrete this can get.

12
00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.333
Companies are bleeding money on inference.

13
00:00:46.633 --> 00:00:51.547
Cut cost forty percent with routing, and fifty percent or more with prompt caching.

14
00:00:51.547 --> 00:00:54.033
That is a budget line, not a nice-to-have.

15
00:00:55.233 --> 00:00:56.700
Now, your specific edge.

16
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.433
Most engineers can only code a feature.

17
00:00:59.733 --> 00:01:02.200
Most architects can only draw diagrams.

18
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:08.433
You are aiming at the rare overlap: design the architecture and write the async Python that executes it.

19
00:01:09.633 --> 00:01:12.967
So lead with the architecture story, and close with the code.

20
00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:14.800
Here is how I designed it.

21
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.867
Here is the trace showing it running.

22
00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:18.833
And here is the number it moved.

23
00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:20.804
Let's recap.

24
00:01:20.804 --> 00:01:23.500
Pick one advantage and execute it visibly.

25
00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:26.533
Evals and cost are the most concrete signals.

26
00:01:26.833 --> 00:01:29.100
Be both the architect and the engineer.

27
00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.441
And always show a proof artifact.

28
00:01:31.441 --> 00:01:34.100
Next up: the proof of production portfolio.
